# Command ggshield

## What does this command do:

The ggshield command line tool helps developers detect and prevent vulnerabilities like hardcoded secrets before pushing their code to shared repositories.

## Installed from

For Fedora install using: pipx install ggshield
For Raspberry Pi install using: pipx install ggshield
For Mac install using: brew install ggshield

## Command path

For Fedora run: /home/kinscoe/.local/bin/ggshield
For Raspberry Pi run: ~/.local/bin/ggshield
For Mac run: /opt/homebrew/bin/ggshield

## Command documentation

Docs can be found at https://dashboard.gitguardian.com/workspace/886400/get-started

## Command options

# Authenticate with GitGuardian (required before first use)
ggshield auth login

# Check authentication / API status
ggshield api-status

# Scan a local git repository for secrets
ggshield secret scan repo /path/to/your/repo

# Scan staged changes (pre-commit)
ggshield secret scan pre-commit

# Scan commits about to be pushed (pre-push)
ggshield secret scan pre-push

# Scan a directory or file
ggshield secret scan path /path/to/dir

# Scan a commit range
ggshield secret scan commit-range HEAD~5..HEAD

# Install as a git hook (pre-commit or pre-push)
ggshield install -m pre-commit
ggshield install -m pre-push

# Output results as JSON
ggshield secret scan repo /path/to/repo --format json

# Ignore a detected secret (add to ignore list)
ggshield secret ignore

# Log out
ggshield auth logout
